{
  "0": "Across all four datasets, increase chronological positional embedding contributions from 1.0 to 1.15. The regression at 0.75 motivates testing modestly stronger order information. Keep position IDs, history truncation, appended-mask readout, embeddings, bidirectional backbone, scoring, loss and optimizer fixed. Apply the same positional scaling during training and prediction, retaining one model per category.",
  "1": "Across all four datasets, replace the training-frequency input scale 1 + 0.02*tanh(z) with 1 + 0.02*z/sqrt(1+z*z), where z remains standardized log1p training item counts. This more gradually saturating feature may reduce sensitivity to moderately frequent items while retaining bounded frequency information. Keep padding and mask scales at 1; preserve embeddings, backbone, readout, loss and optimizer. Save the scales in each category’s single checkpoint.",
  "2": "Across all four datasets, increase only the tied real-item embedding radius multiplier from 0.75 to 0.80, retaining the existing vocabulary-dependent radius formula. A modest increase may strengthen item discrimination without changing embedding width or tying. Keep the exclusive mask vector unnormalized, and preserve frequency features, history policy, backbone, scoring formula, loss and optimizer. Use the same effective embedding weights in training and prediction.",
  "3": "Across all four datasets, add label_smoothing=0.02 to the existing full-vocabulary masked-target cross-entropy, retaining temperature 0.8 and global masked-target averaging. Mild smoothing may reduce overconfidence on sparse item observations without the user reweighting that previously regressed. Preserve masking, negative sampling, features, embeddings, backbone, scoring/readout, optimizer, scheduler and batch/epoch settings; retain one model per category."
}
